From 558ac01ac7fbfb545090dbdd656502b572b38e12 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 11:43:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Platform: MLO restart warning, mDNS service types, GT-BE98
 Pro pressure sensor, diagnostics v1.3.62

- MLO: after a soft restart with MLO on, the router checks whether the radios' PCIe link came back and warns (dashboard
  and MLO page) that a power cycle is needed when it did not. The check only counts once the router has logged the
  link line on an earlier start, so a board that words it differently never warns falsely.
- mDNS across networks: chosen service types can be limited on the main reflector too (avahi reflect-core-types).
- GT-BE98 Pro: the pressure sensor driver is built; /bin/ceventd is linked for the event daemon's consumers.
- IPsec: the strongSwan vici plugin is not loaded (nothing uses swanctl).
- Diagnostics v1.3.62: the features of v3.4.9 - v3.8.3 in the report (sections 3c, 4d, 14h), the login redirect
  host and the review seal masked.
- Defaults for the new switches (all off where optional).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
